.TH FL-NIGHTLIGHT 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-nightlight \- warmer screen colours at night
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-nightlight\fR [\fB\-\-print\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shifts the colours of all screens towards red at night, through the
wlr-gamma-control protocol of \fBfl-wm\fR(1). The session starts it
(\fI/etc/xdg/autostart/fl-nightlight.desktop\fR); it follows changes to its
settings right away and fades between day and night. While night light is
off it leaves the screens' colours alone.
.PP
Settings > Displays and the panel's right-click menu turn it on and off.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The \fB[NightLight]\fR section of \fI~/.config/fldesktop/desktop.ini\fR:
.TP
\fBEnabled=\fRfalse
Night light on or off.
.TP
\fBTemperature=\fR4000
The colour temperature at night, 1500 to 6500 kelvin (6500 is neutral).
.TP
\fBSchedule=\fRsunset
\fBsunset\fR: from sunset to sunrise, worked out from the time zone's
location in \fIzone1970.tab\fR (or \fBLatitude=\fR and \fBLongitude=\fR in
degrees); \fBcustom\fR: from \fBFrom=\fR to \fBTo=\fR (HH:MM, default 20:00
to 07:00); \fBalways\fR: all the time. The change fades in over 30 minutes
(45 around sunset and sunrise).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the colour temperature the screens should have now and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
